-- report.talk: the syntax sketch's 09-http-fetch `fetchOne`, rewritten for
-- ADR 0020's suspending-call rule, plus a use of the text Library.

use pad, padLeft from text
use trim from text as tidy       -- renamed on import

script variable results = {}

on fetchOne s, every time
  report s, "2026-09-27" and wait
  put it into the (s) of results
  -- Was: put report(s, "2026-09-27") into the (s) of results
  -- `report` calls `ask http to get … and wait`, so it may suspend. That
  -- makes a function-style call to it a load error, and the Command Call
  -- must say `and wait`. The result is left in `it`, as after an `ask`.
  if the length of results = 3 then tell log to write "all in: " & results
end fetchOne

-- Functions can never suspend, so this one reads as immediate and is.
function row station, mean
  return pad(tidy(station), 8) & padLeft(mean as text, 6)
end row

-- `report` and `summarise` as in 09-http-fetch.talk, unchanged except that
-- `report` is the Handler called above.
